# The assessment of COR-EXEC-001 against this build. The requirement identifier is this
# file's stem and appears nowhere inside it, because a second place to spell the identity
# is a second place for it to be wrong -- the rule OD-SPEC-007 chose for a record
# registration, and CHK-003.assessment states for this registry.
#
# COR-EXEC-001: "Every correction operation shall declare or derive artifact, symbol,
# configuration, generated-source, dependency, provider-state, and semantic read/write
# sets at the strongest available resolution. Derived sets shall identify the provider,
# guarantee, confidence, and invalidation basis."
#
# ReadWriteSet/ReadWriteResolution/DerivedProvenance are real and tested: all seven named
# resolution tiers, and all four named derived-provenance fields (reusing
# nomos_contracts::ProviderId/Guarantee for the first two). What is not real: "every
# correction operation" does not hold. CorrectionCandidate, the type a correction
# operation actually is in this crate, has no field of this type and constructs nothing
# through it -- ChangeSet::Touched remains the only read/write answer any real candidate
# carries, at Artifact resolution, the weakest tier this type names.
verdict: Partial
site: crates/corrections/nomos-corrections/src/read_write_resolution/read_write_set.rs#ReadWriteSet
gap: crates/corrections/nomos-corrections/src/correction_id/correction_candidate.rs#CorrectionCandidate
